# Secrets. This is the important part of this file.
#
# The config holds RPC URLs with API keys in them, and older ones held seed
# phrases. Nothing that can carry a key goes in git — not once, not "just to get
# started", because git remembers.
config.json
deployments.json
*.key
*.pem
.env
.env.*

# Keystores, if the app is ever pointed at a directory inside the repo. Those
# files are encrypted, but an encrypted key in a repo is still a key in a repo.
keystores/
*.keystore

# Build output. Five gigabytes of it.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Runtime state and cache: session logs, traces, the theme, cached tokens, the
# fill ledger. Machine-local by definition, and the logs record addresses and
# amounts.
.trenches/
.bot/
*.log

# macOS
.DS_Store
hero-*.png

# Vendor documentation kept locally for reference, not redistributed.
pons-v2.txt
/pools.trade/

# Solidity language server scratch — solc input dumps, not source.
.solidity-language-server/

# Local agent tooling config. Machine-local settings rather than project source,
# and this kind of file is where provider API keys end up. It also kept every
# build stamped `-dirty`: build.rs asks `git status --porcelain`, which counts
# untracked files, so one stray directory made the stamp stop meaning
# "uncommitted code".
.codex/

# Foundry build output — regenerated by `forge build`.
cache/
out/
